# C512 model integration after the ordinary and full-block scans

This is a later activation runbook. The v35 model remains unchanged while the ordinary GEMM scan runs. First finish the 10,376-case ordinary scan, review its exported policy and rebuild. Then rerun the local C512 proof on that new binary and measure the complete 4,128-case C512 full-block domain against the resulting ordinary GEMM baseline. The earlier v35 local proof cannot establish the identity of a later build. Use the existing C512 activation runbook with fresh release/output names for that second scan.

Only after the C512 scan and its no-op resume audit pass should the measured C512 policy and later model/helper patch be activated. The scanner's pre-integration interception deliberately requires the old QKV-linear/attention route; it must not be rerun after the model hook as though it still measured the same baseline.

## Review and activate the later patch

The exact later sources are listed in `outputs/c512_qkv_model_hook_manifest.json.draft`. Its four production files are `dlssnr/inference.py`, `tools/vendor_global_block.py`, `tools/vendor_trunk.py` and `tools/native_benchmark.py`; the fifth entry is the new prepared-hook test. Root owns copying, rebuilding and the exclusive GPU slot. No command in this draft has been executed on a GPU by its author.

Before copying, check the recorded active-base SHA256 values. If a base has changed, rebase the small intended hunks rather than copying an old complete file. `tools/materialize_c512_qkv_hook.py.draft` preserves unchanged UTF-8 bytes and original mixed line endings; it rejects stale bases and never writes active files. It also preserves the unrelated arrow in the native CLI help text. The separate audit helper and its tests may be activated as `tools/audit_c512_qkv_native_rows.py` and `tests/test_c512_qkv_native_metadata_audit.py`; the test prefers the active helper and falls back to the draft before activation.

The prepared cache is an owned deployment snapshot. Its canonical tensor is a view of cache slice zero. Copy and assign state-dict loads restore that alias even when every incoming key was independently cloned. Conflicting canonical/cache values and canonical-only updates to a cached block fail instead of leaving stale packed weights. A cache-only load with `strict=False` can replace the complete snapshot. Change trainable weights on the source model and prepare a new snapshot to regenerate packed data. The load error is local to the affected block, matching normal PyTorch's lack of whole-model rollback.

Copy the reviewed generated `sm_120_c512_qkv.json.draft` and `c512_qkv_policy.h.draft` into their production policy paths, rebuild and install using the established release snapshot procedure. Preserve the exact extension and source snapshot. Freeze all active C++/model/tuning/native files for the following checks and native journal. The Python model only names a fixed network operand/operator; C++ retains all shape/device/variant decisions.

## Record the installed identity and run local integration checks

Use a unique release label instead of `postscan` when more than one integration attempt exists. The identity script imports the extension and reads compiled diagnostics without launching a GPU kernel.

```powershell
Set-Location D:\Research\DLSSNR-PyTorch
@'
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,importlib.util,json
from dlssnr import ops
import torch
root=Path.cwd()
binary=Path(importlib.util.find_spec('dlssnr._C').origin)
digest=lambda p:hashlib.sha256(Path(p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()
paths=['dlssnr/inference.py','tools/vendor_global_block.py','tools/vendor_trunk.py','tools/native_benchmark.py','csrc/kernel_launcher/c512_qkv_policy.h']
data=dict(extension_path=str(binary),extension_sha256=digest(binary),compiled_c512_qkv_policy_version=torch.ops.dlssnr.compiled_c512_qkv_policy_version(),compiled_gemm_policy_version=torch.ops.dlssnr.compiled_gemm_policy_version(),source_sha256={p:digest(root/p) for p in paths})
(root/'outputs/c512-postscan-identity.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
print(json.dumps(data,indent=2))
'@ | & .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Identity collection failed' }
$c512Release = Get-Content -Raw outputs/c512-postscan-identity.json | ConvertFrom-Json
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/test_c512_qkv_policy_cpu.py tests/test_c512_qkv_prepared_hook.py::CPUHookTests tests/test_c512_qkv_native_metadata_audit.py -q --junitxml=outputs/c512-postscan-cpu.xml
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'C512 integration CPU checks failed' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/test_c512_qkv_public_dispatch.py tests/test_c512_qkv_prepared_hook.py -q --junitxml=outputs/c512-postscan-gpu.xml
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'C512 integration GPU checks failed' }
$c512Sanitizer = (Get-Command compute-sanitizer).Source
& $c512Sanitizer --tool memcheck --target-processes all --launch-timeout 300 --error-exitcode 86 --log-file outputs/c512-postscan-memcheck.log .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/test_c512_qkv_public_dispatch.py tests/test_c512_qkv_prepared_hook.py -q --junitxml=outputs/c512-postscan-memcheck.xml
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'C512 integration memcheck failed' }
& $c512Sanitizer --tool racecheck --kernel-name kns=c512_qkv_attention --target-processes all --launch-timeout 300 --error-exitcode 87 --log-file outputs/c512-postscan-racecheck.log .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/test_c512_qkv_attention.py::test_mutable_capture_alignment_current_stream tests/test_c512_qkv_attention_prefetch.py::test_mutable_capture_alignment_current_stream tests/test_c512_qkv_public_dispatch.py::test_mutable_graph_current_stream_and_snapshot tests/test_c512_qkv_prepared_hook.py::test_later_helper_matches_public_snapshot_and_mutable_capture -q --junitxml=outputs/c512-postscan-racecheck.xml
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'C512 integration filtered racecheck failed' }
$env:DLSSNR_FULL_MODEL_TEST = '1'
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe run_tests.py -q --junitxml=outputs/c512-postscan-fullsuite.xml
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Full integration suite failed' }
```

The later hook contributes five CPU tests and 64 parameterized GPU cases covering all sixteen real C512 weights, packed/Half activation storage and copy/assign state-dict loading. Public dispatch tests separately check the ordered oracle, the three actual resolution anchors, FP16 fallback, malformed operands and mutable capture. The helper/model comparison establishes identical prepared routes and immutable snapshots; it is not by itself an independent arithmetic oracle.

Memcheck is unfiltered. Racecheck is intentionally bounded to the two C512 fused kernel names. The other operators and composition-only cases still execute correctness checks, but their GPU accesses are outside that race filter. Keep the incomplete v35 unfiltered attempt separate; it is not passing race evidence. A measured policy may select composition for a particular small mutable-graph case, so private incumbent/prefetch mutable-capture tests remain in the command to exercise both kernel names regardless of policy.

## Complete-network anchor timings

```powershell
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tests/benchmark_model.py --prepared --packed-activations --precision fp8 --valid 1280x720 --valid 1920x1080 --valid 3840x2160 --warmups 3 --repeats 15 --output outputs/model-c512-postscan-fp8.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Prepared packed model benchmark failed' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tests/benchmark_model.py --prepared --precision fp16 --valid 1280x720 --valid 1920x1080 --valid 3840x2160 --warmups 3 --repeats 15 --output outputs/model-c512-postscan-fp16.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Prepared FP16 model benchmark failed' }
```

This is whole candidate-network forward timing with eager/graph equality. It does not measure the native renderer or a DLL call. The model report currently pins the extension but does not name the C512 policy version, so retain `c512-postscan-identity.json` alongside it and verify its extension digest matches the benchmark report. Compare like-for-like graph timing with the prior release; do not add component gains or subtract timings collected under different conditions.

## Native trunk smoke, range and no-op resume

Use fresh output paths and journals. Both direct endpoint adapters remain inside candidate timing. The original path uses pinned SM120 cubins and chained global attention. Run the geometry audit first; the current default 720p/1080p/4K IDs are 0/212/900, but use the reported IDs if the manifest changes.

```powershell
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools/native_range_audit.py --output outputs/c512-postscan-domain.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Native geometry audit failed' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe run_tuning.py native-range --execute --families trunk --packed-activations --trunk-io direct --native-attention chained --geometry-ids 0 212 900 --output outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan-smoke.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE -notin 0,2) { throw 'Native smoke execution failed' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools/native_range_audit.py --report outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan-smoke.json --allow-selected --require-complete --expected-binary-sha256 $c512Release.extension_sha256 --output outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan-smoke-audit.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Native smoke proof audit failed' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools/audit_c512_qkv_native_rows.py --report outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan-smoke.json --expected-binary-sha256 $c512Release.extension_sha256 --require-cache --output outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan-smoke-cache-audit.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Native smoke C512 preparation audit failed' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe run_tuning.py native-range --execute --families trunk --packed-activations --trunk-io direct --native-attention chained --output outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE -notin 0,2) { throw 'Native full range execution failed' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools/native_range_audit.py --report outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan.json --require-complete --expected-binary-sha256 $c512Release.extension_sha256 --output outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan-audit.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Native full range proof audit failed' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools/audit_c512_qkv_native_rows.py --report outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan.json --expected-binary-sha256 $c512Release.extension_sha256 --require-cache --output outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan-cache-audit.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Native full range C512 preparation audit failed' }
$c512JournalBefore = (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan.sqlite3 -Algorithm SHA256).Hash
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe run_tuning.py native-range --execute --families trunk --packed-activations --trunk-io direct --native-attention chained --output outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE -notin 0,2) { throw 'Native no-op resume failed' }
if ((Get-FileHash -LiteralPath outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan.sqlite3 -Algorithm SHA256).Hash -ne $c512JournalBefore) { throw 'Native no-op resume modified journal bytes' }
& .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools/native_range_audit.py --report outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan.json --require-complete --expected-binary-sha256 $c512Release.extension_sha256 --output outputs/native-trunk-c512-postscan-noop-audit.json
if ($LASTEXITCODE) { throw 'Native no-op proof audit failed' }
```

Use `--require-cache` when the generated SM120 table contains at least one fused choice: preparation should then create the QKV cache for all sixteen C512 blocks, including rows whose phase/M selects the composition guard. Omit it only for a deliberately all-composition policy. The row audit also rejects any nonzero compiled choice with a missing cache, mismatched shapes/phase/M, broken alias attestation or conflicting helper/policy hashes. Its variant fields are compiled predictions from saved actual operands, explicitly not a kernel trace.

Native exit status 2 can mean a completed, correct run that misses the speed gate. The coverage audit must still pass and the report's speed failures must remain visible. Compare the no-op audit's committed-record digest and policy/source identity with the first audit. Complete native coverage here means 931 geometries covering every integer input width 1280–3840 and height 720–2160. The timed scope is resident blocks 1–69 with matched physical endpoints and required adapters. The NGX host, renderer, preprocessing block 0 and final block 70 are outside this scope. Neither these timings nor the local scan establish the requested 85% hardware-utilization gate.
